{
  "date": "2026-10-08",
  "title": "What Happens When Somebody Disagrees?",
  "tagline": "Disagreement doesn’t only reveal what we think. It can reveal what we’ve attached to being right.",
  "headline": "What Happens When Somebody Disagrees?",
  "headline_sub": "Defending Truth or Defending Ego?",
  "slug": "when-somebody-disagrees",
  "series": "The Battle Before the Battle",
  "category": "Leadership & Culture",
  "seo_title": "Handling Disagreement Without Getting Defensive | TheWrkShop",
  "seo_description": "Disagreement is not automatically dishonor. A biblical leadership lesson on listening, teachability and leading people who see things differently.",
  "keywords": [
    "leadership",
    "disagreement",
    "conflict",
    "teachability",
    "defensiveness",
    "team culture",
    "Christian leadership"
  ],
  "og_image": "/assets/og/when-somebody-disagrees.png",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "James 1:19-20",
      "text": "“Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak and slow to become angry, because human anger does not produce the righteousness that God desires.”"
    },
    {
      "ref": "Proverbs 18:13",
      "text": "“To answer before listening, that is folly and shame.”"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Someone disagrees with you."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Before you’ve finished hearing them, something starts happening."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Your body tightens.",
            "You prepare your response."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You search for the weakness in their argument."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You stop listening to understand."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You begin listening to:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WIN."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s Battle Before the Battle territory."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because the argument you eventually have may have started several moments earlier."
        },
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "steps": [
            "Disagreement.",
            "Threat.",
            "Interpretation.",
            "Defensiveness.",
            "Counterargument.",
            "Escalation."
          ],
          "caption": "The visible conflict came later.",
          "link": {
            "href": "/upstream/",
            "text": "See the full framework"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "THE BATTLE STARTED WHEN DISAGREEMENT BECAME DANGER."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“IF HE DISAGREES WITH ME, I NEED TO DEFEND MYSELF.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes truth absolutely needs defending."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "What exactly am I defending?",
            "Truth?",
            "Or ego?",
            "Conviction?",
            "Or reputation?",
            "Biblical faithfulness?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Or my need to be seen as intelligent?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WE SAY WE’RE DEFENDING TRUTH WHEN WE’RE ACTUALLY DEFENDING OURSELVES."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s why James tells us:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "quick to listen.",
            "slow to speak.",
            "slow to anger.",
            "That order matters."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "DISAGREEMENT IS NOT AUTOMATICALLY DISHONOR."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Someone can disagree with you and love you."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Correct you and respect you.",
            "Question your conclusion without questioning your worth."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And sometimes the brother who loves you most is the one willing to say:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I DON’T THINK YOU’RE SEEING THIS CLEARLY.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If every disagreement feels like betrayal, correction becomes almost impossible."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And a man who cannot be corrected eventually becomes difficult to disciple."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "what_kind_of_room_are_we_building",
      "label": "What Kind of Room Are We Building?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Imagine a room where everybody agrees because disagreement is costly."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s not necessarily unity."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "It may simply be:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "COMPLIANCE."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Biblical unity does not require identical opinions about everything."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Brotherhood should be strong enough for:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "“I see that differently.”",
            "“Help me understand.”",
            "“I think you’re wrong.”",
            "“You may be right.”",
            "“I need to think about that.”",
            "“I was wrong.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Those are healthy sentences."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "listening_can_be_an_act_of_humility",
      "label": "Listening Can Be an Act of Humility",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Proverbs warns against answering before listening.",
            "Why?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because listening says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I MAY NOT YET HAVE ALL THE INFORMATION.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "That’s humility.",
            "It doesn’t mean surrendering conviction."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "It means conviction doesn’t need insecurity to protect it."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes after listening carefully you’ll still say:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“I disagree.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But now:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "you understood before answering.",
            "That’s different."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_battle_before_the_battle",
      "label": "The Battle Before the Battle",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When challenged, ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Why did that feel threatening?",
            "What am I afraid this disagreement means?",
            "That I’m wrong?",
            "Weak?",
            "Uninformed?",
            "Disrespected?",
            "Not in control?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "DOES BEING WRONG ABOUT SOMETHING THREATEN WHO I AM?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If my identity is secure in Christ, correction may sting."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But it doesn’t have to destroy me."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "dont_miss_this",
      "label": "Don’t Miss This",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Being teachable does not mean believing everyone who corrects you."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Some criticism is inaccurate.",
            "Some advice is foolish."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Some disagreements are theological matters where conviction must remain firm."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Discernment still matters."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But teachability says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I CAN EXAMINE WHAT YOU SAID WITHOUT NEEDING TO DESTROY YOU FOR SAYING IT.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s maturity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "WHAT HAPPENS INSIDE ME WHEN SOMEONE DISAGREES?",
            "DO I LISTEN OR PREPARE MY DEFENSE?",
            "WHAT AM I PROTECTING?",
            "CAN PEOPLE CLOSE TO ME SAFELY TELL ME THEY THINK I’M WRONG?",
            "WHEN WAS THE LAST TIME I SAID:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“YOU WERE RIGHT. I WAS WRONG.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The next time disagreement comes:",
            "Don’t rush."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Ask one more question before making your argument."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“HELP ME UNDERSTAND WHAT YOU MEAN.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Then listen.",
            "You may still disagree."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But don’t let insecurity answer before wisdom has listened."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "A man who cannot be corrected eventually becomes difficult to disciple."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Father,",
            "Make me teachable."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Slow me down when disagreement feels threatening."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Show me when I am defending truth and when I am simply defending ego."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Give me courage to hold conviction without becoming defensive."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Give me humility to say:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“I was wrong.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Build brotherhood strong enough for disagreement without division."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And let truth matter more to me than winning."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "The battle can start when disagreement becomes danger."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "We can say we’re defending truth when we’re actually defending ourselves."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Disagreement is not automatically dishonor."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Agreement produced by fear isn’t necessarily unity. It may simply be compliance."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "A man who cannot be corrected eventually becomes difficult to disciple."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "I can examine what you said without needing to destroy you for saying it."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
